    entries: [
      {
        tag: 'Added',
        title: 'Memory writes topic chapters that keep their identity',
        body: 'Facts that cluster around one topic are now written up as a chapter — and the chapter survives its own growth. When new facts join, the grown cluster supersedes its old chapter instead of minting a parallel copy, and a chapter can never be absorbed into a cluster built from its own members. Topics only relate on two independent signals — embedding similarity plus a shared salient token, never similarity alone. One caveat carried from the changelog: the eval\'s passing verdict holds under its standard grounding rule and flips under a stricter one — disclosed as such, not hidden.',
